      lab1_stage1_motor_test/lab1_stage1_motor_test.ino _hostcheck/main.cpp -o _hostcheck/test.exe

full simulation (virtual alphabot physics + scripted serial scenarios):
  build: g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -I_hostcheck -include _hostcheck/Arduino.h -x c++ ^
      lab1_stage1_motor_test/lab1_stage1_motor_test.ino _hostcheck/sim_main.cpp -o _hostcheck/sim.exe
  run:   _hostcheck/sim.exe
  result: 26/26 PASS (direction check x6 modes, dead band search, coast 38mm vs brake 5mm
          run-on, garbage input ignored)

sim internals (Arduino.h):
  - virtual alphabot model lives IN Arduino.h so the .ino TU links against it
  - all mutable sim state is `inline` (C++17), NOT static - static gives each TU its own
    copy and the sim silently reads a different world than the sketch writes (cost an afternoon)
  - channel B nominal forward = IN3=0/IN4=1 per the guide's table (swapping = wheels fight)
  - model params at top of Arduino.h: WHEEL_D_MM, TRACK_MM, SLOTS, DEADBAND_PWM, ASYM_R...
    replace with academy measurements as they are taken

hint: two msys64 installs on PATH (C:\msys64 and C:\STM32\msys64) - if g++ exits 1 with no
      output, run with PATH="/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin:$PATH" first
